{
  "_about": "Named figures owned by MODEL_BEHAVIOUR.md that the shape-matching guard cannot see: bare integers. Each has a value, the committed artefact it is read from, and the exact phrase each file states it in. ML/graphsentinel_v2/tests/test_figures_guard.py holds every phrase to the value and every value to its artefact. To change a figure: change the artefact, then this file, then the phrases.",
  "_why_phrases": "Do not simplify this to 'the file contains the value'. A bare 12 or 8 appears in almost any file, so that check passes whatever the file says. Two checks constrain together and neither does alone: value against artefact (the number is the measured one) and phrase against file (the sentence carrying it is still there, with that number in it).",
  "_artefact_pointer": "A file, then the keys to follow. A dict step selects the rows of a table that match it; the key after it is read from each row. A dict or list left at the end is summed.",
